-- Clout Couture's Waterfront Mansion (owner, Oct 21: "go"; content/shop/clout-couture.json), part 1:
--   * Ten plots on Billionaire's Row, the Astoria waterfront (lib/map/landmarks.ts "billionaires-row"). A purchase takes
--     the lowest free plot (mansion_plots); a refund frees it (and its edition number is never reissued, 0102), so the
--     piece is sold out only while all ten plots are taken.
--   * The owner can live in it: a home ('waterfront_mansion', owners only) whose weekly rent is its upkeep, the priciest
--     Astoria rent, so it never saves money compared with a C$ home (lib/economy.ts topAstoriaRent; tick bills it like any
--     rent, and eviction works as for any home). Moving in costs the first week (no broker for your own mansion). A
--     refund while living there moves the player to the cheapest home.
--   * Lola announces each new owner (a News item, names through the chat word filter).
--   * couture_map() also returns the mansions by plot, with the gate's name (the Studio can hide it, as for the yacht).

